      "comment": "PRETTY PANAMA (7) put in a much better performance last start when in the placings at Geelong behind Aston Monsoon (23.13) in a Grade 5. Has the early speed to land on the pace and can stick on. Good form should continue. PACIFIC POPPY (4) took the sit on the lead from a low draw but levelled up and led around the bend to score (23.09) at this track in a T3 RSTW over 400m. Leading chance again. ATHENIAN GODDESS (8) jumped from a middle draw last time and could manage only fourth and beaten 4.5 lengths (17.16) at Healesville. Has a good record here at this journey. Can do much better this time. WARRIOR JACK (6) cannot be ruled out.",
